      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Generation Source**\n\nI'm zeroing in on Google Cloud's Generative AI as the platform. The next step is embedding its unique identifier within the Python script to establish the connection for streaming the model outputs.\n\n\n**Establishing the Code Base**\n\nI'm now drafting the Python script, `stream_platform_generation.py`, which is the essential core. I've decided to leverage the `vertexai` SDK, specifically the preview version. I'm now adding the initialization of the Vertex AI SDK and the model specification, aiming to use a model like \"gemini-pro.\" My focus now is on implementing the streaming functionality to capture and print model responses.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789887133854,
          "start": 1789887131573
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bd962fb5001qwFlaVvkurCPhw",
